The image, Figure 6, displays flow cytometry histograms illustrating the impact of Nano-11 on costimulatory molecule expression by dendritic cells (DCs). Compared to medium control (gray line), incubation with Nano-11 (black line) for two days notably enhanced the surface expression of CD80 and CD86 on DCs, and to a lesser extent, CD40. This upregulation of costimulatory molecules signifies the activation of DCs, a critical step for initiating an effective adaptive immune response. These findings directly support Nano-11's role as an immunostimulatory adjuvant, as detailed in the study's in vitro DC activation experiments.